IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc27-s746-parole.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 746 to 746.1 (time in custody counted towards a life sentence's period without eligibility
-- for parole; the bar on parole, day parole and absences until all but three years, or all but one fifth for a person under 18, have been served).
-- Section 747 is shown repealed (nothing to encode).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
-- Answers are `MAYBE BOOLEAN` (or a MAYBE of a type): JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING elsewhere.

§ `Section 746 -- Time spent in custody`

DECLARE `s 746 purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 746 section 745`
    `s 746 section 745.1`
    `s 746 section 745.4`
    `s 746 section 745.5`
    `s 746 section 745.52`
    `s 746 section 745.6`
    `s 746 another purpose`

DECLARE `s 746 case` IS ONE OF
    `s 746(a) a sentence of imprisonment for life after July 25, 1976`
    `s 746(b) a sentence of death that has been or is deemed to have been commuted to a sentence of imprisonment for life`
    `s 746 a sentence of another kind`

-- src:16239 | 746 In calculating the period of imprisonment served for the purposes of section 745, 745.1, 745.4, 745.5, 745.52 or 745.6, there shall be included any time spent in custody between
-- src:16240 | (a) in the case of a sentence of imprisonment for life after July 25, 1976, the day on which the person was arrested and taken into custody in respect of the offence for which that person was sentenced to imprisonment for life and the day the sentence was imposed; or
-- src:16241 | (b) in the case of a sentence of death that has been or is deemed to have been commuted to a sentence of imprisonment for life, the day on which the person was arrested and taken into custody in respect of the offence for which that person was sentenced to death and the day the sentence was commuted or deemed to have been commuted to a sentence of imprisonment for life.
@ref s 746 (src:16239-16241)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 746 purpose`
      case IS A `s 746 case`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 746 the time spent in custody is included in calculating the period of imprisonment served` MEANS
    IF purpose EQUALS `s 746 another purpose` OR case EQUALS `s 746 a sentence of another kind`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In calculating the period of imprisonment served for the purposes of section 745, 745.1, 745.4, 745.5, 745.52 or 745.6" and the two cases (a) and (b)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:16240 | (a) in the case of a sentence of imprisonment for life after July 25, 1976, the day on which the person was arrested and taken into custody in respect of the offence for which that person was sentenced to imprisonment for life and the day the sentence was imposed; or
@ref s 746(a) (src:16240)
GIVEN `the day the sentence of imprisonment for life was imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 746(a) the sentence is a sentence of imprisonment for life after July 25, 1976` MEANS
    IF `the day the sentence of imprisonment for life was imposed` GREATER THAN (Date 25 7 1976)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a sentence of imprisonment for life after July 25, 1976" (a scope limit with no "only", ruling (c))

-- The days in custody: from the day of the arrest to the day the sentence was imposed (case (a)) or commuted (case (b)).
-- The text says "any time spent in custody between" the two days; the days are counted as the difference of the two dates, so the last day is not counted (fork F-11).
-- src:16240 | (a) in the case of a sentence of imprisonment for life after July 25, 1976, the day on which the person was arrested and taken into custody in respect of the offence for which that person was sentenced to imprisonment for life and the day the sentence was imposed; or
-- src:16241 | (b) in the case of a sentence of death that has been or is deemed to have been commuted to a sentence of imprisonment for life, the day on which the person was arrested and taken into custody in respect of the offence for which that person was sentenced to death and the day the sentence was commuted or deemed to have been commuted to a sentence of imprisonment for life.
@ref s 746 (src:16240-16241)
GIVEN `the day the person was arrested and taken into custody in respect of the offence` IS A DATE
      `the day the sentence was imposed or commuted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 746 the days spent in custody that are included` MEANS
    IF `the day the sentence was imposed or commuted` LESS THAN `the day the person was arrested and taken into custody in respect of the offence`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence cannot come before the arrest in the cases the section names
    ELSE JUST ((DATE_SERIAL `the day the sentence was imposed or commuted`) MINUS (DATE_SERIAL `the day the person was arrested and taken into custody in respect of the offence`))   -- the difference of the two dates: the later day is not counted (fork F-11)

§ `Section 746.1 -- Parole prohibited`

-- src:16243 | 746.1 (1) Unless Parliament otherwise provides by an enactment making express reference to this section, a person who has been sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to this Act shall not be considered for parole or released pursuant to a grant of parole under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act or any other Act of Parliament until the expiration or termination of the specified number of years of imprisonment.
@ref s 746.1(1) (src:16243)
GIVEN `the person has been sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Parliament has otherwise provided by an enactment making express reference to section 746.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the specified number of years of imprisonment has expired or been terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 746.1(1) the person is barred from being considered for parole or released pursuant to a grant of parole` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person has been sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to this Act`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who has been sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to this Act"
        IF `Parliament has otherwise provided by an enactment making express reference to section 746.1`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless Parliament otherwise provides by an enactment making express reference to this section" (fork F-13)
        IF `the specified number of years of imprisonment has expired or been terminated`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the expiration or termination of the specified number of years of imprisonment" (the "until" bar of ruling (d) of 2026-11-05: JUST TRUE before, JUST FALSE after)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 746.1 kind of release` IS ONE OF
    `s 746.1 day parole`
    `s 746.1 an absence without escort`
    `s 746.1 an absence with escort, other than for medical reasons or to attend judicial proceedings or a coroner's inquest`
    `s 746.1 an absence with escort for medical reasons or to attend judicial proceedings or a coroner's inquest`
    `s 746.1 a release of another kind`

-- What the bar covers while it lasts, in subsections (2) and (3): paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) are the same in both.
GIVEN kind IS A `s 746.1 kind of release`
      `the Parole Board of Canada approves the absence with escort` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 746.1 the kind of release is barred while the bar lasts` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 746.1 day parole` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)
    WHEN `s 746.1 an absence without escort` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b)
    WHEN `s 746.1 an absence with escort, other than for medical reasons or to attend judicial proceedings or a coroner's inquest` THEN
        IF `the Parole Board of Canada approves the absence with escort`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except with the approval of the Parole Board of Canada" (fork F-13)
        ELSE JUST TRUE   -- (c)
    WHEN `s 746.1 an absence with escort for medical reasons or to attend judicial proceedings or a coroner's inquest` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (c) bars an absence with escort "otherwise than for medical reasons or in order to attend judicial proceedings or a coroner's inquest"
    WHEN `s 746.1 a release of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraphs (a) to (c) name three kinds

-- src:16245 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), in respect of a person sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to this Act, until the expiration of all but three years of the specified number of years of imprisonment,
-- src:16246 | (a) no day parole may be granted under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act;
-- src:16247 | (b) no absence without escort may be authorized under that Act or the Prisons and Reformatories Act; and
-- src:16248 | (c) except with the approval of the Parole Board of Canada, no absence with escort otherwise than for medical reasons or in order to attend judicial proceedings or a coroner’s inquest may be authorized under either of those Acts.
@ref s 746.1(2) (src:16245-16248)
GIVEN `the person has been sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was convicted of first degree murder or second degree murder and was under the age of eighteen at the time of the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the specified number of years of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER
      `the years of imprisonment served` IS A NUMBER
      kind IS A `s 746.1 kind of release`
      `the Parole Board of Canada approves the absence with escort` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 746.1(2) the kind of release is barred until the expiration of all but three years` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person has been sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to this Act`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a person sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to this Act"
        IF `the person was convicted of first degree murder or second degree murder and was under the age of eighteen at the time of the commission of the offence`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (3)": for a person under eighteen, subsection (3) decides
        IF `the years of imprisonment served` AT LEAST (`the specified number of years of imprisonment` MINUS 3)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the expiration of all but three years of the specified number of years of imprisonment" (the "until" bar: gone once all but three years are served)
        OTHERWISE `s 746.1 the kind of release is barred while the bar lasts` kind `the Parole Board of Canada approves the absence with escort`

-- src:16250 | (3) In the case of any person convicted of first degree murder or second degree murder who was under the age of eighteen at the time of the commission of the offence and who is sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to this Act, until the expiration of all but one fifth of the period of imprisonment the person is to serve without eligibility for parole,
-- src:16251 | (a) no day parole may be granted under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act;
-- src:16252 | (b) no absence without escort may be authorized under that Act or the Prisons and Reformatories Act; and
-- src:16253 | (c) except with the approval of the Parole Board of Canada, no absence with escort otherwise than for medical reasons or in order to attend judicial proceedings or a coroner’s inquest may be authorized under either of those Acts.
@ref s 746.1(3) (src:16250-16253)
GIVEN `the person was convicted of first degree murder or second degree murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was under the age of eighteen at the time of the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of imprisonment the person is to serve without eligibility for parole, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the years of imprisonment served` IS A NUMBER
      kind IS A `s 746.1 kind of release`
      `the Parole Board of Canada approves the absence with escort` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 746.1(3) the kind of release is barred until the expiration of all but one fifth of the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person was convicted of first degree murder or second degree murder` AND `the person was under the age of eighteen at the time of the commission of the offence` AND `the person is sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to this Act`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person convicted of first degree murder or second degree murder who was under the age of eighteen at the time of the commission of the offence and who is sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole for a specified number of years pursuant to this Act"
        IF (`the years of imprisonment served` TIMES 5) AT LEAST (`the period of imprisonment the person is to serve without eligibility for parole, in years` TIMES 4)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the expiration of all but one fifth of the period of imprisonment the person is to serve without eligibility for parole" (the "until" bar: gone once four fifths are served)
        OTHERWISE `s 746.1 the kind of release is barred while the bar lasts` kind `the Parole Board of Canada approves the absence with escort`
